@ [prior_catalogue_assessment] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Weaver_Planner_Identity_Operation_Catalogues_Assessment_2026-08-04.sop
@ [semantic_fabric] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\SOP_Semantic_Fabric_Graph.sop
@ [build_authority] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Engine_Neural_Fabric_CLI_Build.sop

& [FormationIdentity]
  + [specification_uuid] is 4f1336b4-715f-4f29-a413-339ce93534f1
  + [profile] is cantor-semantic-anchor-catalogue/0.1
  + [status] is canonical_formation_implementation_not_activated
  + [purpose] is give Cantor an inspectable compiled semantic addressing surface that unfolds exact SOP records from terms and intended use
  + [compact_rule] is associations propose, boundaries filter, signatures admit, hashes resolve, proof explains

& [AuthorityInvariant]
  + authoritative meaning remains solely in recognized admitted compiled SOP packages and their exact semantic records
  + every catalogue is derived from and bound to one immutable admitted fabric generation
  + every retained candidate resolves through an exact SemanticAddress before its content can be returned
  + catalogue entries association contributions rankings and continuations grant no truth authority capability permission or effect authority
  + stale or incompatible catalogue and router roots fail closed
  + source file and line locators aid people while stable identities and content digests govern machines
  - never: treat the catalogue learned weights lexical similarity graph proximity or fluent model selection as a second source of truth

& [CatalogueIdentity] is the immutable projection identity
  + [profile] is the exact catalogue protocol
  + [catalogue_id] is stable logical identity
  + [catalogue_root] is the digest of normalized catalogue contents
  + [fabric_root] is the exact admitted semantic-fabric generation
  + [package_root_set] is the sorted admitted package identities and digests
  + [compiler_identity] is the deterministic projection implementation and version
  + [derivation_proof] records inputs normalization ordering and output digest
  + [created_from_logical_revision] is supplied data and not a live-clock claim

& [SemanticAddress] is the only catalogue target identity
  + [unit_id] is stable semantic identity
  + [unit_digest] is immutable compiled unit content
  + [package_id] and [package_digest] bind the recognized owner
  + [kind] is the exact semantic record family
  + [context_identity] binds interpretation scope and purpose domain
  + [version] binds admitted lifecycle identity
  + [source_anchor_refs] bind file clause span and span digest
  + [display_locators] may include current path and line for inspection
  = must: resolve exactly against the same admitted fabric root before content projection

& [IdentityAnchorEntry] is the table-of-contents record
  + [address] is one SemanticAddress
  + [preferred_expression] and [alias_set] are compiled naming forms
  + [kind] distinguishes entity concept role proposition contract file program faculty resource state observation result fault and other admitted families
  + [meaning_ref] identifies exact meaning content rather than duplicating mutable paraphrase
  + [purpose_set] and [use_case_set] declare intended relevance without universal applicability
  + [context_set] preserves scope assumptions perspective world and ambiguity
  + [included_boundary_set], [excluded_boundary_set], and [protected_identity_set] preserve identity edges
  + [relation_ref_set] preserves typed adjacency without merging endpoints
  + [authority_scope] and [lifecycle] preserve signer scope status version supersession staleness and revocation
  + [source_anchor_refs] preserve exact provenance
  = must: sort by SemanticAddress identity rather than display spelling

& [OperationAnchorEntry] is the operation-index record
  + [address] is one admitted operation SemanticAddress
  + [preferred_expression], [verb_set], [alias_set], and [phrase_set] are compiled retrieval forms
  + [operation_class] is relation observation query inference transformation validation control capability or physical effect
  + [role_signature] names subject object context instrument authority evidence and output roles as applicable
  + [input_type_constraints] and [output_type_constraints] bind accepted identity kinds and schemas
  + [preconditions], [invariants], [postconditions], and [failure_conditions] preserve transition semantics
  + [authority_requirements], [effect_class], [reversibility], [risk], [cost], [resource_budget], and [time_horizon] constrain application
  + [applicability_refs] bind declared seams and [non_transfer_set] prevents unlicensed property authority and evidence transfer
  + [source_anchor_refs] and [lifecycle] preserve exact authority
  - never: make a verb match imply capability invocation or effect permission

& [ApplicabilityBinding] is the typed identity-operation seam
  + [binding_id] is content-addressed
  + [operation_ref] and [role_ref] identify the exact operation role
  + [identity_ref_or_kind] identifies an exact subject or admitted identity family
  + [context], [purpose], [conditions], and [boundary_refs] state where the binding may hold
  + [evidence_refs] and [source_anchor_refs] state why the binding exists
  + [transfer_law] and [non_transfer_set] preserve endpoint identities and prohibited inheritance
  + [authority_ref] remains a separately verified requirement
  + [status] is declared derived candidate contradicted blocked stale or unresolved
  = must: keep candidate status distinguishable from admitted declaration

& [AssociationChannel] is a closed proposal family
  + [exact_identity] is direct stable-address equality
  + [exact_label] is compiled preferred-expression or alias equality
  + [declared_applicability] is an admitted ApplicabilityBinding whose guards are separately evaluated
  + [typed_relation] is a bounded allowed path through exact relation identities
  + [lexical] is deterministic text-derived relevance
  + [embedding] is approximate vector-derived relevance
  + [learned_route] is a router-artifact proposal bound to catalogue and fabric roots

& [AssociationContribution] is one inspectable proposal reason
  + [channel] is one AssociationChannel
  + [candidate_address] is the proposed exact target
  + [basis] preserves matched term label binding relation path text calculation or model output
  + [channel_local_value] preserves value domain scale normalization and ordering semantics
  + [evidence_refs] preserve supporting and contradictory evidence
  + [model_identity] is required only for model-produced contribution
  + [conditions] and [unresolved_guards] preserve applicability limits
  + [status] is proposed retained excluded contradicted stale incompatible or clipped
  - never: use one contribution as authority or silently translate its value into another channel's semantics

& [AnchorQuery] is the bounded semantic-address request
  + [profile] and [request_id] bind protocol identity
  + [term_set] preserves original input terms
  + [subject], [purpose], and [use_case_set] bind intended meaning
  + [include_boundary_set] and [exclude_boundary_set] bind scope
  + [known_identity_set] optionally supplies exact caller anchors
  + [requested_detail_set] names identity operation applicability relationship definition clause condition instruction evidence authority fault source or derivation needs
  + [allowed_relation_set] and [maximum_depth] bound traversal
  + [allowed_channel_set] explicitly enables proposal mechanisms
  + [authority_context] binds caller read scope separately from relevance
  + [budget] bounds candidates records paths bytes elapsed proxy and continuation count

& [AnchorCandidate] is one gated resolution prospect
  + [address] is the exact target
  + [contribution_set] preserves every material proposal channel and basis
  + [priority_tier] is exact_identity exact_label declared_applicability typed_relation lexical embedding or learned_route
  + [channel_local_rank] compares candidates only under declared compatible semantics
  + [eligibility] is eligible excluded ambiguous contradicted unknown stale unauthorized unresolved or clipped
  + [unresolved_guards] and [omission_refs] remain visible
  + [exact_resolution_required] is always true

& [PriorityLattice] prevents score laundering
  + exact identity precedes exact compiled label
  + applicable declared bindings follow only after context condition and boundary evaluation
  + allowed typed relation paths follow under their path policy
  + lexical embedding and learned channels extend recall only when requested
  + one tier sorts by its declared channel-local order then stable address
  + lower-tier numeric magnitude cannot outrank a retained higher tier
  + winning-tier ties remain explicit ambiguity
  + evidence confidence risk cost and authority remain separate accounts and never become relevance arithmetic

& [AnchorQueryResult] is the proof-carrying catalogue return
  + [profile], [request_id], [catalogue_root], and [fabric_root] bind the exact exchange
  + [candidate_set] is ordered under PriorityLattice
  + [record_projection] contains only requested exact-resolved detail
  + [relationship_path_set] identifies every traversed relation and endpoint
  + [boundary_account] separates admitted excluded ambiguous contradicted unknown stale unauthorized unresolved and clipped material
  + [association_account] groups contributions by channel without merging their semantics
  + [source_anchor_set] and [proof] bind packages units spans gates paths exclusions and omissions
  + [continuation] is a root-bound bounded opaque cursor when eligible material remains
  + [result_digest] commits the normalized response

& [DeterministicPipeline] is the mandatory execution order
  * validate request profile authority context closed fields and budgets
  * select one admitted fabric root and exactly matching catalogue root
  * normalize terms while preserving originals and exact supplied identities
  * gather exact identity then exact-label contributions
  * apply lifecycle authority subject purpose use-case context and boundary gates
  * exact-join declared applicability records
  * expand allowed typed relations within all budgets
  * optionally gather lexical then compatible approximate or learned proposals
  * apply PriorityLattice and preserve winning ambiguity
  * exact-resolve each retained SemanticAddress against admitted records
  * project only requested details relationships source anchors omissions and proof
  * compute result digest and optional root-bound continuation
  - never: skip an earlier exact or boundary gate because a later channel is confident

& [FacultyContract]
  + Observer binds subject purpose consequence and disposition
  + Honesty validates identity meaning provenance ambiguity evidence polarity status and truthful score labels
  + Security validates roots recognition authority scope boundaries constraints budgets and effect isolation
  + Weaver proposes typed identity-operation bindings paths compositions and incompatibilities without selection authority
  + Planner orders bounded searches and later procedure transitions under prerequisites and stop conditions
  + Refiner selects the smallest sufficient projection without deleting material qualification
  + Scribe records input contributions gates paths omissions proof digest and correction lineage

& [FaultSet]
  + [CATALOGUE_ROOT_MISMATCH] rejects a projection not bound to the active fabric
  + [ADDRESS_UNRESOLVED] rejects a candidate absent from exact admitted records
  + [SOURCE_PROOF_GAP] rejects a requested authoritative projection lacking package unit or source proof
  + [AMBIGUOUS_ANCHOR] retains tied identities without arbitrary collapse
  + [CONTEXT_OR_BOUNDARY_MISMATCH] excludes a candidate outside declared use
  + [UNAUTHORIZED_ANCHOR] excludes readable relevance from caller authority
  + [CHANNEL_INCOMPATIBLE] rejects cross-channel arithmetic or an incompatible learned artifact
  + [SCORE_LAUNDERING] rejects relevance represented as confidence truth authority risk or permission
  + [BUDGET_CLIPPED] returns bounded partial evidence and continuation rather than pretending completeness

& [RequirementSet] is SAC-001 through SAC-024
  + [SAC-001] derive every catalogue from one exact admitted fabric generation
  + [SAC-002] make catalogue root package roots compiler and derivation proof inspectable
  + [SAC-003] define exact SemanticAddress resolution
  + [SAC-004] define IdentityAnchorEntry as table-of-contents view
  + [SAC-005] define OperationAnchorEntry as operation-index view
  + [SAC-006] preserve typed ApplicabilityBinding and non-transfer law
  + [SAC-007] keep authoritative records outside disposable derived projections
  + [SAC-008] distinguish every AssociationChannel
  + [SAC-009] preserve contribution basis value semantics evidence conditions model and status
  + [SAC-010] enforce PriorityLattice without cross-channel scalar collapse
  + [SAC-011] keep evidence confidence risk cost and authority separate from relevance
  + [SAC-012] bind subject purpose use case boundaries detail channels relations authority and budgets in AnchorQuery
  + [SAC-013] return exact candidates compact requested records boundary account association account source proof omissions continuation and digest
  + [SAC-014] preserve ambiguity contradiction unknown stale unauthorized unresolved and clipped states
  + [SAC-015] resolve every retained candidate through exact admitted fabric lookup
  + [SAC-016] rebuild or reject on any governing generation change
  + [SAC-017] prove deterministic byte identity for equal inputs
  + [SAC-018] prove mutations of roots addresses sources channels order gates and digests fail closed
  + [SAC-019] prove overlapping exact behavior agrees with existing proof-carrying query
  + [SAC-020] measure self-hosted corpus size latency allocations response bytes recall ambiguity and proof completeness before optimization
  + [SAC-021] bridge semantic addresses to later attention procedure requests without conflating checkpoint identity
  + [SAC-022] require a reviewed labeled corpus baseline metrics abstention and zero gate bypass before learned routing
  + [SAC-023] keep provider persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA and Minecraft behavior separately governed
  + [SAC-024] preserve all seven faculty accounts for consequential candidate disposition

& [GraduationPlan]
  + [slice_1] closed pure machine forms canonical encoding digest validators and fixtures
  + [slice_2] deterministic derivation from existing admitted SemanticFabric
  + [slice_3] exact identity label context applicability and typed-relation scan
  + [slice_4] lexical boundary result proof compact projection and query equivalence
  + [slice_5] self-hosted corpus artifacts measurements and operator views
  + [slice_6] provider-free semantic-address to attention-procedure bridge
  + [slice_7] separately activated shadow learned router only after adoption prerequisites
  = must: activate and prove one contiguous slice before its dependent

